            0.209
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Different materials absorb and heat up differentl y"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.444,
            0.202,
            0.89,
            0.394
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "under sunlight. You have already learnt Grade 7 how land heats up faster than water. Curiosity There may be some variation due to Chapter 7 the material forming the land and the colour of the soil. Dark surfaces absorb more sunlight, while light coloured surfaces reflect more and remain comparatively cooler. For example, dark coloured roads heat up more quickly, while light coloured surfaces remain comparatively cooler. You have also learnt why dark coloured clothes feel hotter than white ones in summer."
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.809,
            0.213,
            0.886,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": [
            {
