        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.819,
            0.89,
            0.906
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "From Table 13.1, you must have seen that snow and ice have high albedo, meaning they reflect a large proportion of the incoming solar radiation. This makes polar regions very cold. On the other hand, surfaces like black soil and ocean water have lower albedo as they absorb more solar radiation, and hence, they are relatively warmer."
            }
          ]
